  "origin": "Project Gutenberg provides books that are not protected under US copyright law. Dolma processes all Gutenberg books (downloaded April 3, 2023, extracted with GutenbergPy). ~4.8B tokens, 52k documents. Per the Dolma datasheet's representativeness discussion, Gutenberg books are mostly from the public domain (at the time of publication, books published before 1927). The license field carries the CC Public Domain Mark and the licenseScope field qualifies the jurisdiction dependence — the same pattern as the Pleias Common Corpus Gutenberg record, demonstrating that the licenseScope field (folded into 0.0.1 after the Common Corpus stress test) generalizes cleanly to a second corpus's Gutenberg component. The Dolma datasheet notes AI2 did not contact Project Gutenberg; the books are obtained directly from gutenberg.org. See notes/stress-test-olmo-dolma.md.",
